<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@type": ["HomeAndConstructionBusiness", "LocalBusiness"], "@id": "https://sandstonestucco.ca/#organization", "name": "Sandstone Stucco Co", "url": "https://sandstonestucco.ca", "logo": {"@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://sandstonestucco.ca/images/og-image.webp"}, "priceRange": "$$", "telephone": "(403) 555-0148", "email": "info@sandstonestucco.ca", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "addressLocality": "Calgary", "addressRegion": "AB", "addressCountry": "CA"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 51.0447, "longitude": -114.0719}, "areaServed": [{"@type": "City", "name": "Calgary", "addressRegion": "AB"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Northeast Calgary", "addressRegion": "AB"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Northwest Calgary", "addressRegion": "AB"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Southwest Calgary", "addressRegion": "AB"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Southeast Calgary", "addressRegion": "AB"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Airdrie & Chestermere", "addressRegion": "AB"}, {"@type": "City", "name": "Cochrane & Okotoks", "addressRegion": "AB"}], "@context": "https://schema.org", "description": "Stucco repair in Calgary for cracks, hail damage, flicker holes and parging. An independent contractor quotes after seeing the wall. Call (403) 555-0148.", "image": "https://sandstonestucco.ca/images/og-image.webp", "hasOfferCatalog": {"@type": "OfferCatalog", "name": "Stucco Repair Services", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Stucco Repair & Crack Patching"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Parging Recoats"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Hail & Woodpecker Damage"}}, {"@type": "Offer", "itemOffered": {"@type": "Service", "name": "Re-Stucco & Recoating"}}]}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite", "@id": "https://sandstonestucco.ca/#website", "url": "https://sandstonestucco.ca", "name": "Sandstone Stucco Co", "publisher": {"@id": "https://sandstonestucco.ca/#organization"}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "How does stucco repair pricing and scoping work?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The contractor sees the wall first, then writes a scope and a price, because the same crack can be a small patch or a moisture problem. Calgary firms publish very different ranges for similar jobs. For example, Calgary Parging lists small patch repairs at $550 to $1,125 before GST, while Martini Stone Masonry lists minor hairline crack repairs at $500 to $1,500 (GST not stated). Treat published figures as context, not a quote, and see the <a href=\"/stucco-repair-cost-calgary/\">cost guide</a> for the detail."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How fast will someone respond, and how long does a repair take?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "This site cannot promise a response time or a start date, because each independent contractor sets its own schedule. Calgary Parging says most repairs take 1 to 3 days. Calgary Stucco and Slate says some repairs take two trips and some up to four, with up to weeks in between so each layer cures. Bigger jobs take longer, and the season limits when work can be done."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does Sandstone Stucco Co do the stucco work?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. It is an advertising service paid by independent contractors, and it holds no licence, insurance or warranty. The contractor who visits quotes and contracts with you directly. Ask that contractor about their Calgary business licence, WCB coverage and any warranty, and get the details in writing."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "I have hail damage. What should I do about my insurance?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Contact your home insurance provider before any repair work, as the City of Calgary advises. The Insurance Bureau of Canada says hail damage is typically covered by home insurance, but check your own policy. A contractor can write a repair estimate that you may pass to your insurer. This site does not file, negotiate or manage claims."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I fill or repair a woodpecker hole myself?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Northern flickers are federally protected, so do not harm the bird or disturb a hole with eggs or chicks in it. Environment and Climate Change Canada says you may discourage a bird from returning with measures that cause it no harm, such as covering the area with wire mesh. Once nesting has ended, a contractor can patch and reinforce the hole."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can stucco be repaired in winter in Calgary?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Often not well. Imasco's guide specification says to do no traditional stucco work when air and substrate temperatures are below 4 degrees C for 24 hours before, during and after application, and ADEX specifies 5 degrees C or above for 24 hours. Calgary Parging says off-season repairs need heated hoarding. In winter a contractor can still survey the wall, quote it and book the work for spring."}}]}</script>
