<!-- PROCESS -->
<section style="padding:76px 24px;background:#F3ECE1;">
  <div style="max-width:1020px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
    <span class="kicker">How It Works</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,38px);margin:0 0 44px;">Three Steps: Photo, Quote, Repair.</h2>
    <div class="steps-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:32px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:34px 26px;box-shadow:0 4px 18px rgba(42,37,33,0.08);">
        <div style="width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:50%;background:#A4491F;color:#fff;font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:0 auto 16px;">1</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">Enquiry and technical discussion</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Call or send the form and describe what you see: hail marks, a flicker hole, a crack, a bulge or crumbling parging. Photos help. If it is hail damage, contact your home insurance provider before any repair work, as the City of Calgary advises.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:34px 26px;box-shadow:0 4px 18px rgba(42,37,33,0.08);">
        <div style="width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:50%;background:#A4491F;color:#fff;font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:0 auto 16px;">2</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">Site survey and scope</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">The contractor looks at the wall, works out whether it is cement stucco or EIFS and checks for signs of moisture. One Calgary firm notes that nobody can tell the full extent of water damage until the wall is opened up, so scope can change.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:16px;padding:34px 26px;box-shadow:0 4px 18px rgba(42,37,33,0.08);">
        <div style="width:54px;height:54px;border-radius:50%;background:#A4491F;color:#fff;font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin:0 auto 16px;">3</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 10px;">Written proposal, then the work</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">You get a written proposal to compare and can accept it or not. Timing follows the weather: one Calgary firm puts the stucco season at April through October, and repairs outside it need heated hoarding.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
